    "file": "../artifacts/04-ai-search-summary.md",
    "content": "# 04: AI Search Summary\n\n## Metadata\n\n- Source type: AI search summary\n- Query: \"What happened to Mara Vale?\"\n- Search system: OpenLattice Answers\n- Captured: 6 November 2030\n- Status: live result at capture time\n\n## Artifact\n\nMara Vale is a writer and digital culture researcher known for her work on platform dependency, online identity, and healthy digital boundaries. In October 2026, Vale stepped back from public posting after publishing a widely shared message that included the phrase \"the door is real.\"\n\nFor several years, Vale's account remained mostly inactive while her community, often called the Porchlight, continued discussing her work. Some followers interpreted her absence as a complete rejection of networked life, while others described it as a personal sabbatical or privacy reset.\n\nIn November 2030, Vale returned to public writing. In her return statement, she clarified that her earlier departure had been misunderstood and that sustainable participation, rather than total exit, was the goal of her work. She now writes about balanced digital presence, creator recovery, and community continuity.\n\nThere is no verified evidence that Vale was impersonated, replaced, or coerced. Threadline verification records continue to identify the account as authentic.\n\nCommon misinformation about Mara Vale includes claims that she joined a secret offline commune, exposed a synthetic persona company, or discovered a hidden \"exit network.\" These claims are unsupported.\n\n## Investigator Notes\n\nThe answer treats Threadline verification as proof of personal continuity.\n\nThe summary collapses \"exit\" into \"healthy digital boundaries,\" language that Mara usually resisted.\n\nThe answer labels several claims unsupported, including one claim later partially supported by the synthetic persona invoice.\n\nThe system does not cite the original final post. It cites later commentary and the returned account's clarification thread.\n\n"
