    "file": "../artifacts/06-welcome-back-comments.md",
    "content": "# 06: Welcome Back Comments\n\n## Metadata\n\n- Source type: comment thread\n- Platform: Threadline\n- Parent post: `@maravale`, 4 November 2030 comeback post\n- Capture window: first 6 hours\n- Status: partial export\n\n## Artifact\n\n### sisterstatic\n\nI am shaking. I kept your last post printed inside a book for four years. I do not know what to do with the fact that you are here.\n\nWelcome home, Mara.\n\n### Sable_3\n\nTHANK YOU for saying this. Some of us were harmed by the romance of leaving. Some of us cannot just vanish into a cottage and call it liberation.\n\n### formedlight\n\n\"I no longer think every door opens only one way\" is going to stay with me for a long time.\n\n### LioLeftEarly\n\nI was angry when you left. I am still angry. I am also relieved in a way that makes me embarrassed. Both things are true.\n\n### RafiK\n\nI need people to slow down.\n\nThis account is verified. That does not mean we have heard from Mara.\n\nPlease do not harass Elian. Please do not turn doubt into sport. But please, please slow down.\n\n### candleindex\n\nRafi, respectfully, she literally sounds exactly like herself.\n\n### lowtable\n\nDoes she? The sentences are right but the temperature is wrong.\n\n### brightbreaks\n\nFour years changes people. We begged her to come back and now that she is back people are calling her fake because she healed in a direction they do not like.\n\n### hearthcache\n\nI keep waiting for a pause. That is probably unfair. Nobody owes us the same room forever.\n\n### SeraNox\n\nMara's return is a gift to everyone working toward humane continuity online. We can honor exit without fetishizing absence. Welcome back.\n\n### NorthPassenger\n\nI do not trust anyone who uses Mara's name and \"continuity\" in the same sentence.\n\n### Threadline Context\n\nThis conversation is receiving unusually high engagement from users who do not follow `@maravale`.\n\nFor safety, replies may be ranked to reduce speculation about private identity, location, or medical status.\n\n## Investigator Notes\n\nThe community is not fooled all at once. It is divided between relief and unease.\n\nSera Nox appears early and frames the return through \"humane continuity,\" language associated with synthetic representation vendors.\n\nThreadline's context label turns uncertainty about personhood into a safety problem.\n\nThe strongest acceptance comments are not naive. They come from people with real losses attached to Mara's absence.\n"
