    "file": "../artifacts/14-tier-six-clue.md",
    "content": "# 14: Tier Six Clue\n\n## Metadata\n\n- Source type: physical-world clue\n- Origin: scan of handwritten notice and library checkout slip\n- Location: redacted coastal town\n- Date range: 2027-2030\n- Provided by: anonymous local source\n- Status: partially redacted\n\n## Artifact\n\n### Community Noticeboard Scan\n\nWednesday evenings, back room.\n\nMending, kettle, borrowed tools, forms help, quiet reading.\n\nNo phones on the table.\n\nBring what needs repair.\n\nLeave what needs forgetting.\n\nAsk Jo for the blue key.\n\n### Library Checkout Slip\n\nBorrower name: M. Venn\n\nItems:\n\n- Practical Radio Repair, 1978 edition\n- The Care and Keeping of Hand Tools\n- Local Estuary Birds, revised field guide\n- Oral History Methods for Small Communities\n- The Complete Poems of Lorine Niedecker\n\nDue date: 14 May 2029\n\nFine waived: storm closure\n\n### Handwritten Margin Note\n\nNot proof.\n\nA mercy.\n\nIf someone asks whether she is alive, tell them the soup was too salty and she argued about the chairs.\n\nThat should be enough for anyone who knows what alive means.\n\nJ.\n\n## Investigator Notes\n\nThe clue is deliberately insufficient as public proof.\n\n\"M. Venn\" may be an alias. \"Jo\" likely refers to Jo Bell, a librarian and organizer mentioned in Rafi Kline's private notes.\n\nThe noticeboard phrase \"Leave what needs forgetting\" echoes the deleted blog fragment's idea that rooms can \"forget without deleting.\"\n\nThe artifact points toward Mara's continued embodied life but does not provide enough information to locate her.\n\n"
